      <title-group>
        <article-title>Counting invented widgets: a synthetic JATS fixture</article-title>
      </title-group>
      <abstract abstract-type="graphical">
        <p>GRAPHICAL-ABSTRACT-MARKER should never be chosen over the main abstract.</p>
      </abstract>
      <abstract>
        <p>Widgets were counted weekly at three invented sites for one simulated year.
          Counts rose by four per cent, and two observers agreed closely.</p>
      </abstract>
    </article-meta>
  </front>
  <body>
    <p>LOOSE-BODY-MARKER: a paragraph that sits directly under body.</p>
    <sec id="s1" sec-type="intro">
      <label>1</label>
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p>Widget counting is a stand-in task with no real literature
        <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r1">[1]</xref>. Monthly counts hide short swings
        (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r2">2</xref>, <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r3">3</xref>).</p>
    </sec>
    <sec id="s2" sec-type="methods">
      <title>Methods</title>
      <p>The agreement index was
        <inline-formula><mml:math><mml:mi>FORMULA-INLINE-MARKER</mml:mi></mml:math></inline-formula>
        computed per site.</p>
      <disp-formula id="e1"><mml:math><mml:mi>FORMULA-DISPLAY-MARKER</mml:mi></mml:math></disp-formula>
      <sec id="s2a">
        <title>Observers</title>
        <p>Two observers counted every widget in a fixed square once a week.</p>
      </sec>
